          ],
          "content": "Arithmetic Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "because the value of 10 + 2 = 12 is greater than the value of 7 + 1 =  8. Similarly,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.13,
            0.568,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "1 3 - 2 \\leq 4 \\times 3 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.163,
            0.294,
            0.187
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.19,
            0.849,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": "1. Fill in the blanks to make the expressions equal on both sides of the = sign: (a) 13 + 4 = \\_\\_\\_\\_ + 6 (b) 22 + \\_\\_\\_\\_ = 6 × 5 (c) 8 × \\_\\_\\_\\_ = 64 ÷ 2 (d) 34 – \\_\\_\\_\\_ = 25"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.28,
            0.852,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "2. Arrange the following expressions in ascending (increasing) order of their values. (a) $6 7 - 1 9$ (b) $6 7 - 2 0$ (c) (e) $3 5   \\pm   2 5$ $1 2 0 \\div 3$ (d) $5 \\times 1 1$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.399,
            0.707,
            0.423
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "? Example 2: Which is greater? 1023 + 125 or 1022 + 128?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.425,
            0.648,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "Imagining a situation could help us answer this without finding the values. Raja had 1023 marbles and got 125 more today. Now he has 1023 + 125 marbles. Joy had 1022 marbles and got 128 more today. Now he has 1022 + 128 marbles. Who has more?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.536,
            0.648,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "This situation can be represented as shown in the picture on the right. To begin with, Raja had 1 more marble than Joy. But Joy got 3 more marbles than Raja today. We can see that Joy has (two) more marbles than Raja now. That is,"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.677,
            0.424,
            0.899,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.651,
            0.519,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": "1 0 2 3 + 1 2 5 < 1 0 2 2 + 1 2 8 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.685,
            0.651,
            0.709
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 3: Which is greater? 113 – 25 or 112 – 24?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.711,
            0.653,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": "Imagine a situation, Raja had 113 marbles and lost 25 of them. He has 113 – 25 marbles. Joy had 112 marbles and lost 24 today. He has 112 – 24 marbles. Who has more marbles left with them?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.785,
            0.653,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "Raja had 1 marble more than Joy. But he also lost 1 marble more than Joy did. Therefore, they have an equal number of marbles now. That is,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.864,
            0.498,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": "113-25=112-24.",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.681,
            0.695,
            0.902,
            0.892
          ],
